From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:17:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cron): account nested frame output lengths incrementally
 [daveey]

Nested parameter and command walkers recalculated the total fragment length
for each nested span, even when no break offsets were requested. Repeated
command substitutions, backticks and ANSI-C words therefore made accounting
quadratic within the existing line cap. Keep append-only fragments with a
cached length while preserving plain-list _out_len and walker contracts.

At reviewed PR #2925 head 69e236270b the deterministic 64-KiB operation budget
fails for both walkers and all three span families, with and without breaks
(12 failures). All 16 regression cases pass with this accounting change,
including normalized newline offsets. Complete discovered lifecycle and
arithmetic consumers: 10716 passed across 69 files. No cap/refusal/parser
semantics changes. Fresh independent exact-head review belongs to the
existing landing owner t_60e1b62eed385db5.
